      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand where you're coming from, and I'm truly sorry that this feels so overwhelming. Disillusionment can make everything feel meaningless, and it's natural to feel exhausted when putting that kind of pressure on ourselves. It's important to give yourself permission to step back, rest, and not rush the process. Finding or creating meaning doesn't always require immediate action or perfection; sometimes, it's about small steps and acknowledging your feelings without judgment.\n\nDo you feel comfortable sharing some of the things that mattered to you, even if they're no longer providing the same comfort or guidance? Sometimes revisiting and reshaping our understanding of those experiences can help us piece together something new, or at least provide a different perspective. And remember, it’s okay to explore these feelings with a trusted friend, family member, or professional who can offer support tailored to your needs. You don't have to go through this alone.",
